WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.050
So we've been talking quite a bit over the
last four years, but in particular in the

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:10.010
period leading up to the election and then
since the election when we've seen not 75

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:15.600
million people, as some in the House of Representatives
have been claiming today, but certainly tens

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:23.560
of millions of people fall for the false belief
that the 2020 presidential election was somehow

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.999
stolen from Donald Trump, even though Donald
Trump was the rightful winner.

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:35.280
It's disheartening and concerning and scary
that so many people have fallen for that.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:42.390
And in thinking about how that came to be,
the idea of a shared psychosis is important

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.470
to think about.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:47.420
And there's a very interesting article in
Scientific American, which we're going to

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:55.240
link to on our YouTube channel, which summarizes
some of Dr. Bande XLE views on what moved

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:02.650
Donald Trump's followers to fall collectively
for these delusions and to then also become

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:08.920
violent and behave destructively, as we saw
on January six during the Trump riot in Washington,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.240
D.C..

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.850
And the the answers are widespread and there
are many overlaps between what Dr. Lee says,

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.869
who's been a guest on this program, by the
way, and what we talked about, about magical

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:24.130
thinking several weeks ago.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:30.569
And when Bandele was asked in this interview
in Scientific America, American, what attracts

00:01:30.569 --> 00:01:32.340
people to Trump?

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.759
Dr. Lee says that there are two major emotional
drives.

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:41.259
There's a narcissistic symbiosis.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:46.539
And then there's the idea of shared psychosis
now, narcissistic symbiosis we've sort of

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.719
talked about before.

00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:56.100
And that is described as the developmental
wounds that make the leader follower relationship

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.200
attractive to both the leader.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:05.729
Trump is hungry for people to worship him,
essentially because he lacks self-worth.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:07.409
And we know this to be true.

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:12.799
We know about Trump's relationship with his
father and how, you know, the relationship

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:17.480
between Fred Trump and Donald Trump is not
that different than the relationship we observe

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:23.100
between Trump and his children, in particular
Don Jr., who seems also desperate for his

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:29.040
father's adulation when Trump doesn't really
seem to care that much about his children,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.079
at least in the sort of traditional ways,
as we've seen publicly, that we understand

00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:40.239
that that's that's something that we've identified
relatively early.

00:02:40.239 --> 00:02:46.730
Shared psychosis is very interesting because
what we are essentially talking about is a

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:52.159
national level delusion that is plaguing tens
of millions of people.

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:56.860
Again, not 75 million, not all 75 million
Trump voters are part of this.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.870
But certainly we would look at the polls and,
you know, when 60 percent of Trump voters

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.909
believed up until weeks ago that it is Trump
who would be inaugurated in a week, not Joe

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:09.879
Biden, it certainly afflicts many of them.

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:18.000
And that is, as again, referred to by Dr Bandele,
the infectiousness of symptoms that go beyond

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.959
group psychology.

00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:25.010
We've talked for a long time about how did
those Tea Party people end up supporting in

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.540
2010 candidates who were running on policies
that weren't good for them, running on low

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.250
taxes for the rich, which these people were
never going to be rich.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.409
We understand the group psychology aspect
pretty well.

00:03:36.409 --> 00:03:39.180
Jonathan Haidt, who I've interviewed, has
talked about that.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:46.659
We understand that the when we talk about
shared psychosis, as Dr. Bandele refers to

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:54.660
it, the processes you put in an influential
position, somebody who is afflicted by this

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.660
psychosis.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.900
Now, we don't have to guess, does Trump believe
the delusions or does he repeat them even

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.109
though he doesn't believe them?

00:04:02.109 --> 00:04:03.109
It doesn't matter.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.959
The point is he repeats them and he's in a
position of power.

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:15.099
And then you can see it spread through the
population, through either an emotional bond

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:21.329
that Trump's followers believe they have with
him or the heightening of people already predisposed

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:27.020
to conspiratorial thinking or paranoia or
people with a propensity for violence.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:34.520
And that fully describes the people that ended
up violently storming the Capitol last week.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:39.220
So let's go through, again, all of the different
elements that exist here.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.919
You start with a group of followers of Trump
that on average is more predisposed to violence.

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:44.919
We know that.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:45.919
We know that.

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:51.670
And we know that from looking at the brain
differences essentially between reactionary

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:55.470
right wingers and other groups, we know that
there's more of a predisposition to violence

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.470
there.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.470
There's more paranoia.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:58.470
There's more fear.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:04:59.470
There's more belief that.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:02.180
Other people are out to get you and on and
on and on, so you start with that group.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:05.970
Now, many of those people, even though they
hold those beliefs, they're not going to fall

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.340
for the shared psychosis.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.690
They're not going to believe the delusions
and they are not actually going to go to the

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.130
Capitol and commit violent acts.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:17.169
But then you take that group, that larger
group that just is slightly more predisposed

00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:21.620
to violence, more predisposed to conspiratorial
and paranoid thinking.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:27.349
And then you do a two month campaign where
the leader, the narcissistic leader, repeats,

00:05:27.349 --> 00:05:28.500
repeats, repeats.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:34.200
These delusions about it was stolen and there
were massive dumps of votes.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.520
And this happened in Pennsylvania and in Michigan.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.229
The watchers weren't allowed to see.

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:40.229
And then in Georgia, this.

00:05:40.229 --> 00:05:41.229
Right.

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:42.229
You repeat it, repeat it.

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:45.710
You do two months to that group and you're
going to take some subset section of those

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:49.810
who are going to be infected for lack of a
better term by these ideas that are being

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:53.030
spread by Trump of the theft of the election.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:59.000
And then you get to January 6th, where you
have a group, broadly speaking, more predisposed

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.669
to conspiratorial thinking and also more predisposed
to violence.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:07.500
Not all of them willing to do it in real life.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:11.800
And for two months, you hammer, hammer, hammer
on them, and then you start using terms like

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:17.199
we've got a fight and you literally say we're
going to go down to Pennsylvania, down Pennsylvania

00:06:17.199 --> 00:06:19.100
Avenue, to the Capitol.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.990
And that's how you get what we got last week.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.750
And the the psychology of it is very interesting.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:29.419
I do think that, you know, there are some
who might just write this off and say, well,

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:30.419
OK, yeah.

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:37.420
I mean, you're sort of psychologizing in some
way.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:44.010
What may or may not be inaccurate psychoanalysis,
but I think it can't be written off because

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.910
if we don't understand it, we're going to
have a very difficult time dealing with it.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.590
And by the way, merely understanding it doesn't
actually tell us how to deal with it.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:58.720
But, you know, we talked about this a few
months ago or so where, you know, we I explained

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.670
that to understand why they are willing to
do these things, you have to understand that

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.949
a lot of these Trump supporters believe that
they are at war, they're at war against the

00:07:05.949 --> 00:07:10.419
left and the media and scientists, atheists,
communists, Marxists, the Democrats who stole

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:12.770
the election and on and on.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.440
And in a sense, they idealize violence as
well.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.580
It's not just that they're predisposed to
it.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:22.350
They idealize violence as being implicit,
as implying that they are also courageous.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:25.599
They're willing to take the risk of going
to the Capitol and being violent.

00:07:25.599 --> 00:07:33.430
And when you are at war, a normal way of interacting
with the world evaporates and you justify

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.130
what you're doing.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:41.500
Much like we see militaries justify what,
absent of a theater of war, would be completely

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.120
absurd, immoral behavior.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.550
Lying is obviously valid if you're at war.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.039
Lying is no big deal.

00:07:47.039 --> 00:07:52.240
And what we saw on January 6th was that even
property destruction, violence, storming the

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:58.360
capital, insurrection, et cetera, even that
is justified when you have this belief that

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.979
you're at war and you share the psychosis
with the great leader.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:03.920
So there's a lot there.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.470
And I encourage you to check out the article.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:12.139
And what you very quickly realize is that
there are self reinforcing aspects of this

00:08:12.139 --> 00:08:14.870
that make it very difficult to break people
out of it.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.240
Very, very important thing to understand.

